[38;2;124;124;124mdeterministic bounds.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. The normal distribution actually suggests that |M(n)| > sqrt(n) happens with [0m[38;2;124;124;124mpositive probability (about 32% of the time if σ² = 1), which would actually [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcontradict the Mertens conjecture but not RH (since RH allows n^{1/2+ε}).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the normal distribution is consistent with RH but doesn't imply it.[0m

